1
00:00:00,204 --> 00:00:03,164
(Sheldon:)That seems a fairly efficient arrangement.

2
00:00:03,332 --> 00:00:06,002
(Beverley:)Yes, we think so.
We've both done papers on it.

3
00:00:06,168 --> 00:00:10,588
Mine from a neuroscientific point of view
and his from an anthropological.

4
00:00:10,756 --> 00:00:13,926
(Beverley:)Mine, of course,
was the only one worth reading.

5
00:00:14,093 --> 00:00:15,133
(Leonard(entering on the phone):)Of course.

6
00:00:15,302 --> 00:00:18,762
(Sheldon:)I would very much like
to read about your sex life.

7
00:00:19,598 --> 00:00:23,518
(Beverley:)Well, it's all online or you can order it
from the Princeton University Press.

8
00:00:23,685 --> 00:00:25,895
(Leonard:)Here's your tea, Mother.

9
00:00:26,146 --> 00:00:28,316
(Leonard:)So, what are you guys talking about?

10
00:00:28,482 --> 00:00:31,942
(Sheldon:)The frequency with which your parents
had intercourse.

11
00:00:32,986 --> 00:00:34,696
(Leonard:)Swell.

12
00:00:34,947 --> 00:00:38,867
(Leonard:)If you're lucky, maybe she'll show you
the PowerPoint presentation.

13
00:00:39,034 --> 00:00:40,614
(Beverley:)I'm sorry, it's on my other laptop.

14
00:00:40,786 --> 00:00:42,326
[GROANS]

15
00:00:43,497 --> 00:00:45,247
(Leonard:)So, Mother...

16
00:00:45,416 --> 00:00:47,996
(Leonard:)- ...what's new?
- You'll have to be more specific.

17
00:00:49,628 --> 00:00:51,968
(Leonard:)All right. Uh, what's new with you?

18
00:00:52,339 --> 00:00:56,679
(Beverley:)Oh, well, I've been having some fascinating
menopausal symptoms recently.

19
00:00:56,844 --> 00:01:00,024
Maybe something less personal?

